.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rosregview-list 1  "rosregview-list "
.SH NAME
rosregview\-list \- List the direct subkeys of a key (default: the root), with subkey and value counts. The optional `KEY_PATH` may be a single segment (`ControlSet001`) or a backslash\-separated subpath (`A\\B\\C`). Empty path == the root
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrosregview list\fR [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> [\fIKEY_PATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the direct subkeys of a key (default: the root), with subkey and value counts. The optional `KEY_PATH` may be a single segment (`ControlSet001`) or a backslash\-separated subpath (`A\\B\\C`). Empty path == the root
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]
Output format (`human` is an aligned table, `json` is machine\-readable)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path to a .hiv file (Windows registry configuration unit)
.TP
[\fIKEY_PATH\fR]
Optional key path inside the hive. Use `\\` (escaped as `\\\\` in most shells) to separate levels. Empty/missing → hive root
